The '''2015–16 Saudi Professional League''' (known as the '''[[Abdul Latif Jameel]] Professional League''' for sponsorship reasons) was the 40th season of the [[Saudi Pro League]], the top Saudi professional league for [[association football]] clubs, since its establishment in [[1976–77 Saudi Premier League|1976]]. The season began on 19 August 2015 and ended on 14 May 2016.<ref>{{cite web |title=جدول الدوري |url=http://www.slstat.com/spl2015-2016ar/champtable.php |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160702031743/http://www.slstat.com/spl2015-2016ar/champtable.php |archive-date=2 July 2016 |url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Al-Nassr FC|Al-Nassr]] were the two time [[2014–15 Saudi Professional League|defending champions]], having won their eighth title the season before.<ref>{{cite web |title=النصر بطلاً لدوري جميل 2014 |url=https://www.alriyadh.com/922240}}</ref> The league was contested by the 12 teams from the [[2014–15 Saudi Pro League|2014–15 season]] as well as [[Al Qadsiah FC|Al-Qadsiah]] and [[Al Wehda FC|Al-Wehda]], who joined as the promoted clubs from the [[2014–15 Saudi First Division|2014–15 First Division]]. They replace [[Al-Orobah FC|Al-Orobah]] and [[Al-Shoulla FC|Al-Shoulla]] who were relegated to the [[2015–16 Saudi First Division|2015–16 First Division]].

On 24 April, [[Al-Ahli Saudi FC|Al-Ahli]] secured their third league title and first since [[1983–84 Saudi Premier League|1984]] with two games to spare after defeating second-placed [[Al Hilal SFC|Al-Hilal]] 3–1 at home.<ref>{{cite web |title=الأهلي بطلا للدوري السعودي للمرة الأولى منذ 32 عاما |url=https://arabic.cnn.com/sport/2016/04/25/alahli-alhilal-saudi}}</ref>

[[Hajer FC|Hajer]] were the first team to be relegated following a 1–0 home defeat to [[Al-Ahli Saudi FC|Al-Ahli]] on 17 April.<ref>{{cite web |title="ضربة جزاء" مثيرة أبقت الأهلي في الصدارة وأكدت هبوط هجر |url=https://www.al-jazirah.com/2016/20160417/sp22.htm}}</ref> [[Najran SC|Najran]] became the second and final team to be relegated following a 3–3 draw with [[Al Raed FC|Al-Raed]] on the final matchday.<ref>{{cite web |title=هبوط نجران وفوز الوحدة في الدوري السعودي|url=https://arabic.sport360.com/article/%d9%83%d8%b1%d8%a9-%d8%b3%d8%b9%d9%88%d8%af%d9%8a%d8%a9/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%af%d9%88%d8%b1%d9%8a-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b3%d8%b9%d9%88%d8%af%d9%8a/386315/%d9%87%d8%a8%d9%88%d8%b7-%d9%86%d8%ac%d8%b1%d8%a7%d9%86-%d9%88%d9%81%d9%88%d8%b2-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%88%d8%ad%d8%af%d8%a9-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%af%d9%88%d8%b1%d9%8a-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b3%d8%b9%d9%88%d8%af%d9%8a}}</ref>

==Teams==
Fourteen teams competed in the league&nbsp;– the twelve teams from the previous season and the two teams promoted from the [[2014–15 Saudi First Division|First Division]]. The promoted teams were [[Al Qadsiah FC|Al-Qadsiah]] (returning to the top flight after three years) and [[Al Wehda FC|Al-Wehda]] (returning to the top flight after two years). They replaced [[Al-Orobah FC|Al-Orobah]] (ending their two-year top-flight spell) and [[Al-Shoulla FC|Al-Shoulla]] (ending their three-year top-flight spell).

